<section class="section">

<h2>
The Undiladze Family
</h2>

<p>

Undiladze
(<strong>უნდილაძე</strong>)
is a Georgian historical family whose representatives
rose to important military and political positions
in Safavid Iran.

</p>

<h2>
Origins and History
</h2>

<p>

Georgian and academic sources identify the Undiladzes
as a Georgian noble and feudal family.

</p>

<h2>
Allahverdi Khan
</h2>

<p>

Allahverdi Khan Undiladze was one of the most important
representatives of the family. He rose through the
Safavid military and administrative system and became
a leading political and military figure.

</p>

<h2>
Imam-Quli Khan
</h2>

<p>

Imam-Quli Khan was the elder son of Allahverdi Khan.
He became governor of Fars and one of the most powerful
Safavid commanders.

</p>

<h2>
Daud Khan
</h2>

<p>

Daud Khan was another prominent son of Allahverdi Khan.
He maintained particularly close political relations
with Georgia.

</p>

<h2>
The Family Account of the Rescue of Two Children
</h2>

<p>

The family manuscript
<strong>Choni Chone Buri</strong>
preserves a family account concerning the rescue of
two infant descendants of Imam-Quli Khan during the
persecution of the Undiladze family.

</p>

<p>

According to the family account, the children were
protected by Georgian women and their true identity
remained concealed for generations.

</p>

<p>

Family research connects the continuation of their
line with the Georgian village of Akhche in Fereydan.

</p>

<h2>
Akhche and the Continuation of the Family
</h2>

<p>

Akhche is an important place in the modern family
memory and genealogy of the Undiladze descendants
in Fereydan.

</p>

<h2>
Genealogy
</h2>

<p>

The existing family genealogy is presented as a
separate archival document on this page.

</p>

<h2>
Family Gathering
</h2>

<p>

A major family gathering was held in the Georgian
village of Akhche in Fereydan, bringing together
descendants connected with the Undiladze family.

</p>

<p>

Its purpose was to strengthen family connections
and preserve the history, identity and heritage
of the ancestors for future generations.

</p>

